From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:04:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] msacm.dll16: thunk the driver, format and stream functions to
 msacm32

A table maps 16 bit handles to the 32 bit ACM handles. acmDriverEnum/ID/Details/Open/Close/Priority/Remove, acmMetrics, acmFormatTagDetails/Enum, acmFormatDetails, acmFormatSuggest and the acmStream functions (synchronous streams only) call msacm32. Choose dialogs and filter functions stay unsupported.

Unverified: no 16 bit runtime or compiler is available here, so this is compile-checked only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

diff --git a/dlls/msacm.dll16/msacm.c b/dlls/msacm.dll16/msacm.c
index c1590f8..3d94302 100644
--- a/dlls/msacm.dll16/msacm.c
+++ b/dlls/msacm.dll16/msacm.c
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@
 #include "mmreg.h"
 #include "msacm.h"
 #include "msacmdrv.h"
+#include "wownt32.h"
